   Um... to clarify, this patch isn't primarily intended to make it easier 
to blank scrolls. It's primarily intended to make water hew closer to the 
laws of physics --- e.g., when a vial full of water shatters on top of 
some papers, the papers get wet. :)
   I consider this a case of TDTDNTOE: I'd expect thrown water to work
this way, and it doesn't --- unless you patch the source.

   Of course, I guess it's a bit hypocritical to make that justification
and then leave the old behavior for acid, so I'll get right on that.
What other potions ought to have effects on the stuff under them? 
Polymorph, I guess, and oil, and !Invis and !SeeInvis if the "invisible
objects" patch is applied... any more?
   Poison seems like a stretch; I'd say you have to #dip to get its
effect, because it needs to soak in, or be carefully applied, or both.

